    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The catenoid is the only minimal surface of revolution\n\nAsk which surfaces of revolution are minimal. With profile $(f(u), u)$ — the radius as a function of height — the condition $H = 0$ becomes an ODE,\n\n$$f\\,f'' = 1 + f'^2,$$\n\nand its solutions are\n\n$$f(u) = c\\cosh\\!\\left(\\frac{u - d}{c}\\right),$$\n\nthe **catenary**. So up to scaling and translation there is exactly one: the **catenoid**, the surface got by rotating a hanging chain.\n\n(The plane is the degenerate exception, arising when the axis is perpendicular rather than in the profile plane.)\n\nThis is why a soap film between two coaxial rings is always a catenoid — there is nothing else it could be.\n\n## The associate family\n\nThe catenoid and helicoid were shown in 3.06 to have identical first fundamental forms. That is the shadow of something stronger: they are two members of a **continuous family** of minimal surfaces,\n\n$$X_\\theta = \\cos\\theta\\;\\underbrace{(\\cosh u\\cos v,\\;\\cosh u\\sin v,\\;u)}_{\\text{catenoid}} \\;+\\; \\sin\\theta\\;\\underbrace{(\\sinh u\\sin v,\\;-\\sinh u\\cos v,\\;v)}_{\\text{helicoid}},$$\n\nevery member of which is minimal and isometric to every other. The deformation from $\\theta = 0$ to $\\theta = \\pi/2$ bends a catenoid continuously into a helicoid **without stretching anything** — a physical soap film can be made to perform it.\n\nSince all members are isometric, $K$ is the same function throughout (Theorema Egregium), and since all are minimal, $H = 0$ throughout. What changes is only $\\mathrm{I\\!I}$ — how the surface sits in space.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- Only the catenoid: solve H = 0 for a surface of revolution --- */\nremove(f, dependency)$\ndepends(ff, u)$\nsrev : [ff*cos(v), ff*sin(v), u]$\nHsr : ratsimp( num( Hof(srev, u, v) ) )$\nprint(\"surface of revolution (f(u)cos v, f(u)sin v, u):\")$\nprint(\"   numerator of 2H = \", Hsr)$\nprint(\"   so H = 0 ⟺ f f'' = 1 + f'²\")$\n\nsol : ode2( ff*'diff(ff,u,2) - 1 - 'diff(ff,u)^2 = 0, ff, u )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   ode2 solves f f'' − 1 − f'² = 0:\")$\nprint(\"      \", sol)$\n\n/* Verify the catenary directly */\nremove(ff, dependency)$\ncat_prof : c*cosh((u - d)/c)$\nresid : ratsimp( cat_prof*diff(cat_prof,u,2) - 1 - diff(cat_prof,u)^2 )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   substituting f = c·cosh((u−d)/c):  residual = \", trigsimp(resid), \" ✓\")$\nprint(\"   the catenary, and hence the catenoid, is the only solution.\")$\n\n/* --- The associate family --- */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"--- associate family X_θ = cos θ · catenoid + sin θ · helicoid ---\")$\ncat2 : [cosh(u)*cos(v), cosh(u)*sin(v), u]$\nhel2 : [sinh(u)*sin(v), -sinh(u)*cos(v), v]$\nassoc(th) := ts( cos(th)*cat2 + sin(th)*hel2 )$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"      θ           I                              H          K\")$\nfor th in [0, %pi/6, %pi/4, %pi/3, %pi/2] do block([X, I1],\n  X : assoc(th), I1 : FFF(X, u, v),\n  print(\"   \", float(th), \"   \", I1, \"   \",\n        ratsimp(Hof(X,u,v)), \"   \", ratsimp(Kof(X,u,v))) )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"every member: same I, H = 0, same K — an isometric deformation\")$\nprint(\"through minimal surfaces, from catenoid (θ=0) to helicoid (θ=π/2).\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "surface of revolution (f(u)cos v, f(u)sin v, u):\n   numerator of 2H =\n                     sqrt(ff^2*('diff(ff,u,1))^2+ff^2)\n                      *(-(ff*'diff(ff,u,2))+('diff(ff,u,1))^2+1)\n   so H = 0 ⟺ f f'' = 1 + f'²\n   ode2 solves f f'' − 1 − f'² = 0:\n      [-(%e^-%k1*log(2*%e^%k1*sqrt(%e^(2*%k1)*ff^2-1)+2*%e^(2*%k1)*ff))\n         = u+%k2,\n       %e^-%k1*log(2*%e^%k1*sqrt(%e^(2*%k1)*ff^2-1)+2*%e^(2*%k1)*ff) = u+%k2]\n   substituting f = c·cosh((u−d)/c):  residual =  0  ✓\n   the catenary, and hence the catenoid, is the only solution.\n--- associate family X_θ = cos θ · catenoid + sin θ · helicoid ---\n      θ           I                              H          K\n    0.0     matrix([cosh(u)^2,0],[0,cosh(u)^2])     0     -(1/cosh(u)^4)\n    0.5235987755982988     matrix([cosh(u)^2,0],[0,cosh(u)^2])     0\n   -(1/cosh(u)^4)\n    0.7853981633974483     matrix([cosh(u)^2,0],[0,cosh(u)^2])     0\n   -(1/cosh(u)^4)\n    1.0471975511965976     matrix([cosh(u)^2,0],[0,cosh(u)^2])     0\n   -(1/cosh(u)^4)\n    1.5707963267948966     matrix([cosh(u)^2,0],[0,cosh(u)^2])     0\n   -(1/cosh(u)^4)\nevery member: same I, H = 0, same K — an isometric deformation\nthrough minimal surfaces, from catenoid (θ=0) to helicoid (θ=π/2)."
          ]
        }
      ]
