    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Minimal is not the same as minimising\n\n$H = 0$ says area is **stationary**, not least. The classic demonstration uses the soap film between two coaxial rings.\n\nTake rings of radius $R = 1$ at heights $\\pm h$. The catenoid spanning them has profile $f(u) = c\\cosh(u/c)$ with $c\\cosh(h/c) = 1$, and area\n\n$$A_{\\text{cat}} = 2\\pi c h + \\pi c^2 \\sinh\\!\\frac{2h}{c}.$$\n\nIts competitor is the **Goldschmidt solution**: two flat discs, one in each ring, joined by nothing. That is not a smooth surface, but it *is* a legitimate limit of soap films, and its area is $2\\pi R^2 = 2\\pi$.\n\nTwo things happen as the rings are pulled apart:\n\n- **The catenoid stops being cheapest.** Beyond a certain separation the two discs have smaller total area, even though the catenoid is still a perfectly good minimal surface. It is a critical point that is no longer a minimum.\n- **The catenoid stops existing at all.** The equation $c\\cosh(h/c) = 1$ has solutions only up to a critical $h/R$; past it, no catenoid spans the rings.\n\nPhysically: pull the rings apart slowly and the film thins, then snaps, leaving a disc on each ring. The snap happens at the first threshold, not the second — the film abandons a still-existing minimal surface because a cheaper configuration is available and a perturbation lets it reach it.\n\nBelow we locate both thresholds numerically.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Rings of radius R = 1 at heights ±h.  Need c with g(c) = c·cosh(h/c) = 1.\n   g is NOT monotonic: it falls to a minimum and rises again, so there are\n   two roots when the minimum is below 1, and none when it is above. */\ng(cc_, hh) := float( cc_*cosh(hh/cc_) )$\n\n/* The minimum of g sits where coth t = t with t = h/c; t* ≈ 1.19968. */\ntstar : 1.1996786402577338$\ncmin(hh) := float(hh/tstar)$\ngmin(hh) := g(cmin(hh), hh)$\n\nprint(\"existence: the catenoid spans the rings iff min g ≤ 1\")$\nprint(\"   min of g is at c = h/t*, t* = \", tstar, \"  (the root of coth t = t)\")$\nprint(\"   min value = \", float(cosh(tstar)/tstar), \" × h\")$\nprint(\"   so a catenoid exists iff h ≤ \", float(tstar/cosh(tstar)))$\n\n/* The larger (stable) root lies above c_min, where g is increasing. */\nfind_c(hh) := block([lo, hi, mid, k],\n  if gmin(hh) > 1 then return('none),\n  lo : cmin(hh), hi : 10.0,\n  for k : 1 thru 300 do (\n    mid : (lo + hi)/2,\n    if g(mid, hh) < 1 then lo : mid else hi : mid ),\n  (lo + hi)/2 )$\n\ncat_area(cc_, hh) := float( 2*%pi*cc_*hh + %pi*cc_^2*sinh(2*hh/cc_) )$\ndisc_area : float(2*%pi)$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"R = 1, rings at ±h.   two flat discs always cost \", disc_area)$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"     h        c (neck)     check c·cosh(h/c)   catenoid area   cheaper\")$\nfor hh in [0.2, 0.4, 0.5, 0.5276, 0.6, 0.6627, 0.7] do block([cc_, A],\n  cc_ : find_c(hh),\n  if cc_ = 'none then\n    print(\"   \", hh, \"        —          —             no catenoid exists\")\n  else (\n    A : cat_area(cc_, hh),\n    print(\"   \", hh, \"   \", cc_, \"   \", g(cc_,hh), \"   \", A, \"   \",\n          if A < disc_area then \"catenoid\" else \"TWO DISCS\") ) )$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"two distinct thresholds:\")$\nprint(\"   h ≈ 0.528 — the discs become cheaper, though the catenoid still exists\")$\nprint(\"   h ≈ 0.663 — the catenoid ceases to exist at all\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"Between them the catenoid is a genuine minimal surface that is NOT\")$\nprint(\"area-minimising: a critical point of area which is not a minimum.\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "existence: the catenoid spans the rings iff min g ≤ 1\n   min of g is at c = h/t*, t* =  1.1996786402577337\n                                   (the root of coth t = t)\n   min value =  1.50887956153832  × h\n   so a catenoid exists iff h ≤  0.6627434193491816\nR = 1, rings at ±h.   two flat discs always cost  6.283185307179586\n     h        c (neck)     check c·cosh(h/c)   catenoid area   cheaper\n    0.2     0.9795106030753393     1.0     2.4962763375894945     catenoid\n    0.4     0.9107379942737879     1.0     4.883793201931147     catenoid\n    0.5     0.8483379380949789     0.9999999999999999     5.991796975802281\n       catenoid\n    0.5276     0.8256034231998053     1.0     6.282174882018836     catenoid\n    0.6     0.7450710898521713     1.0     6.999642567621989     TWO DISCS\n    0.6627     0.5577024722041515     0.9999999999999999     7.537499868081443\n        TWO DISCS\n    0.7         —          —             no catenoid exists\ntwo distinct thresholds:\n   h ≈ 0.528 — the discs become cheaper, though the catenoid still exists\n   h ≈ 0.663 — the catenoid ceases to exist at all\nBetween them the catenoid is a genuine minimal surface that is NOT\narea-minimising: a critical point of area which is not a minimum."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Catenoid area against the two-disc area, as the rings separate */\nhs : makelist(float(k/400), k, 4, 264)$      /* up to h = 0.66 */\ncat_pts : [discrete, hs, map(lambda([hh], cat_area(find_c(hh), hh)), hs)]$\ndisc_pts: [discrete, [0.0, 0.70], [disc_area, disc_area]]$\n\n/* Locate the crossover by bisection on (catenoid area − disc area) */\ndiffA(hh) := cat_area(find_c(hh), hh) - disc_area$\nlo : 0.5$ hi : 0.62$\nfor k : 1 thru 200 do block([mid], mid : (lo+hi)/2,\n  if diffA(mid) < 0 then lo : mid else hi : mid)$\nhcross : (lo+hi)/2$\nprint(\"crossover (areas equal)  h = \", hcross)$\nprint(\"existence limit          h = \", float(tstar/cosh(tstar)))$\nprint(\"between them the catenoid exists but costs more than two discs.\")$\n\nplot2d([ cat_pts, disc_pts,\n         [discrete, [hcross, hcross], [0.0, 12.0]],\n         [discrete, [0.6627, 0.6627], [0.0, 12.0]] ],\n       [x, 0, 0.72], [y, 0, 10],\n       [style, [lines,3],[lines,2],[lines,1],[lines,1]],\n       [legend, \"catenoid area\", \"two discs (2π)\",\n                \"areas equal, h ≈ 0.528\", \"catenoid ceases to exist, h ≈ 0.663\"],\n       [xlabel, \"h — half the ring separation (R = 1)\"],\n       [ylabel, \"area\"],\n       [title, \"a minimal surface that stops being the cheapest, then stops existing\"])$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
